4. WITHIN-SERIES test: across the 4 backends on the SAME series, does the best
   forecaster also detect best? (removes series difficulty entirely)
================================================================================================
n = 340 series with all four backends
mean within-series rho(forecast error, VUS-PR) = -0.415  95% CI [-0.480, -0.350]
fraction of series with rho > 0: 23.8%
wrote results/correlation_levels.csv  (within-series rho -0.415 on n=340)

interpretation: a negative mean rho means that, on a given series, the backend that
forecasts it best also tends to detect on it best, which is the opposite of the
mechanism proposed by the prior study (over-accurate forecasting hiding the anomaly).
